  "replacement": "That drew them to the fireside, where the easy-chair had been pulled snugly up and the tea things stood ready at the sitter’s elbow, with the sugar already in the cup. There were several books on a shelf, and one lay open beside the tea things. Utterson was amazed to find it was a copy of a pious work that Jekyll had several times said he greatly esteemed—and it was annotated, in his own hand, with startling blasphemies."
